WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.170
Essentially a struggle problem — it’s
an open ended thoughtful, non-routine problem.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.740
They’re given a situation.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.090
We go outside and they pick a building.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.231
They collect certain data, and using that
data as a group they have to figure out the

00:00:12.231 --> 00:00:13.550
height of the building.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.710
I may or may not give them a couple of hints.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.070
So now Janet, go all the way up to the building,
to the very top.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.070
Be super dramatic.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.759
To like the end of my phone?

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:24.990
Double tap when she’s ready.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.789
When you’re ready let us know and Brendan
will double tap.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:30.519
Especially in math it’s so simple to just
be like, “This is how you do it.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:31.519
Learn this now.”

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:32.660
You’re not going to remember that.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.820
You’re never going to remember it.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.760
How do we increase they’re actually coming
up with a solution to things?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.060
How do they problem solve? 62.1 degrees.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.060
Booyah.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.620
We want them to be able to stand on their
own two feet and prove to somebody else whether

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.989
in school or in life why something is correct
or why something makes sense to them.

